# Right On Time: settings for your own copy (every setting is in the settings table of infra/README.md).
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Every other setting has an own-copy default, so this file holds only the one value a copy needs.
#
# Two settings you may want to add as lines of your .env:
#   DEMO_MODE=on             the sign-in page offers a "Sign in as" list of the sample people
#   IDLE_RESET_MINUTES=0     an own copy resets itself to its starting state after 120 minutes with
#                            no change (the default); 0 turns that reset off
#
# Docker Compose reads it with:  docker compose --env-file .env -f infra/compose.yaml ...
#
# SAMPLE_PASSWORD_SEED makes the password of each sample person (the first 10 characters of a code
# worked out from this seed and the person's email). It needs 16 or more characters.
#
# This value is PUBLISHED. It is not a secret: it opens the made-up people of any copy that still
# uses it, and it is safe only while the copy is reachable from your own computer alone. Before you
# open your copy to other devices (HTTP_BIND), do both. Change it: a new seed stops password
# sign-in with the published one. Turn the access code on: it stops Sign in as and Forgot password.
# The hosted demo uses a different, private value that is never in this repository.
# Do not use this value for anything that holds real data. Change it before setup if you want
# different sample passwords. Setup writes the passwords once, so change it before the first setup.
SAMPLE_PASSWORD_SEED=right-on-time-sample-seed-2026
